{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Jacob came shalem.</b> He came to Shalem, which is one of the cities of Shechem, whose prince ruled the land, as in ״and they came Bet Lechem.״ <b>The city of Shechem</b> — as in ״the city of Sihon.״ Another interpretation: שלם is the city of Shechem — since his daughter Dinah was violated there, he wanted to note that he came shalem (whole) as far as Shechem. And it is not correct to say that this שלם is Jerusalem, like ״and Melchizedek king of שלם,״ for we do not find that Shechem ruled over Jerusalem." "<b>And he camped facing the city.</b> Because his possessions were many, it was convenient for him to stay outside the city."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:18.871052330Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}